# f1 = f
# `second.setUint8` is read for a call that stands behind its operands, so the read alone opens a guess only where its proof outlives the stretch. That was so where the turn may begin again in the closed copy,
# which `first.setUint8` has ended by storing: the read stayed as written, on the usual way, and cut the walk of the typed copy short. `second` stands in front of the loop and no other code has run in the turn:
# the test whether it is as made is asked in front, and its proof outlives the stretch all the same. 99 instructions a turn | 40.
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK: isInLoop=true isLoopHead=true:
# CHECK: isInLoop=true isLoopHead=true:
# CHECK-NOT: calleeKey=
# CHECK: inlineBuiltin=DataViewSet
